// Title: System Network Connections Discovery - Linux
// Author: Daniil Yugoslavskiy, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-19
// Level: low
// Description: Detects attempts to discover system network connections via common Linux utilities.
// Adversaries may use tools such as netstat, ss, or lsof to enumerate active connections,
// open ports, and listening services on a compromised system.
// MITRE Tactic: Discovery
// Tags: attack.discovery, attack.t1049
// Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_system_network_connections_discovery.yml
// False Positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/lsof" or FolderPath endswith "/netstat" or FolderPath endswith "/sockstat" or FolderPath endswith "/ss"